---
layout: tutorial
title: Create function
description: Add paid app subscription plans to your app with Stripe and Appwrite Functions.
step: 3
---

Head to the [Appwrite Console](https://cloud.appwrite.io/console) and create a new project if you haven't already. If this is your first time using Appwrite, you will be asked to sign up first.

## Find the template {% #find-template %}

Once inside your project, switch to the **Functions** page from the left sidebar and open the **Templates** tab. Use the search bar to look for `subscriptions`, and you will find the **Subscriptions with Stripe** template. Click the template card, then click **Create from template**.

{% only_dark %}
![Subscriptions with Stripe template](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/dark/templates-stripe-subscription.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Subscriptions with Stripe template](/images/docs/tutorials/subscriptions-with-stripe/templates-stripe-subscription.avif)
{% /only_light %}

## Configure function {% #create-function %}

Under **Details**, you can customize the function's **Function name**, **Function ID**, and **Runtime**, or leave them as they are. Keep **Public** turned on, since Stripe and the demo app call the function without an Appwrite session.

The function's domain is generated from its name, for example `subscriptions-with-stripe.fra.appwrite.run`. You will need this domain in the next step.

Leave **Connect later** selected. Appwrite deploys the template's code directly, so you don't need a Git repository for this tutorial. If you'd like to manage the code in your own repository, you can select **Connect your repository** instead, or connect one later from the function's settings.

## Configure variables {% #configure-variables %}

Under **Template variables**, fill the `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` variable with the secret key you copied from Stripe's **API keys** page.

Similarly, fill the `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` variable with the signing secret you copied after creating the webhook.

You don't need to create an Appwrite API key. The template sets the scopes the function needs, and Appwrite passes a short-lived API key with those scopes to every execution.

## Deploy {% #deploy %}

Click **Create and deploy**. Appwrite creates the function and builds its first deployment. Once the build finishes, you will see the function's domain, which you can visit with **Open URL**.
